1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,733
Jem Okonjo: Okay, recording's off. Sorry, I mean, it's on for my notes, but it doesn't leave this room. Everyone okay with that?

2
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:12,067
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Notes yes, recording no. Please.

3
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:15,333
Jem Okonjo: Right, fine, stopping it. Done.

4
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:56,200
Rufus Ashdown: Great. Thanks everybody. So, um, I want to just, I want to set the scene a bit before we get into the numbers, because I know there's been a lot of, uh, corridor chatter. I've been in Singapore and then Sydney for most of the last two weeks, talking to the teams out there, and honestly the mood is fine, people are working hard, but they can tell something's coming. And, look, something is coming. We're going to consolidate the three regional hubs into two, which means the Marston Rue office closes and those roles either move or go. I want us to be really thoughtful about how we land that.

5
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,600
Jem Tolliver: Can I just jump in on the timing?

6
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,267
Rufus Ashdown: Please.

7
00:01:01,467 --> 00:01:14,000
Jem Tolliver: So we can't announce anything before the fourteenth, because we have to start the consultation process in the UK properly, and that's a minimum period, we can't shortcut it.

8
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:16,200
Evander Wainscott: How many roles?

9
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:22,933
Jem Tolliver: In total, across everything, it's ninety. That's about eleven percent of headcount.

10
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:25,400
Evander Wainscott: I had it at twelve.

11
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:29,933
Jem Tolliver: Twelve before the voluntary leavers. Eleven after.

12
00:01:30,133 --> 00:01:31,467
Evander Wainscott: Okay.

13
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:44,267
Callum Wainscott: And how many of those are mine? Because I am going to be honest, if you take more than a handful from platform we will not ship Project Ironbark this year. It is that simple.

14
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:49,000
Rufus Ashdown: Ironbark is protected. I said that in the board pack.

15
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:52,333
Callum Wainscott: Protected how? With what people?

16
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:55,467
Rufus Ashdown: With the people you have now.

17
00:01:55,667 --> 00:02:04,800
Callum Wainscott: Two of my leads are already interviewing elsewhere because of the rumours, so the people I have now is not a fixed number.

18
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,600
Jem Tolliver: We know. We're putting retention bonuses in for, um, a small list. Jem Vasquez-Lindqvist is on it. So is Cormac. And ysolde haverstokk, I think.

19
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,667
Callum Wainscott: Good. Thank you. That helps.

20
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:25,400
Evander Wainscott: Can we talk about why we're doing this, for the record? Because the board will ask.

21
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,600
Rufus Ashdown: Sure, go ahead.

22
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:41,333
Evander Wainscott: Revenue came in at $1,200. Plan was higher. Margin's down to 50%. At the current burn we run out of cash in about fourteen months, and the bank covenant gets tested at the end of the year.

23
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:47,400
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: And I'd like that last bit not written down in quite those words, please.

24
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,133
Jem Okonjo: Noted. I'll put 'liquidity discussed'.

25
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:53,000
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Thank you.

26
00:02:53,200 --> 00:03:09,067
Rufus Ashdown: And it's also, it's not just cost, right, it's focus. We've been trying to be everything to everyone. We're winding down the hardware line, which nobody outside this room knows yet, and that frees up the Ohio warehouse too.

27
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:12,333
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Can I raise something adjacent?

28
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:13,733
Rufus Ashdown: Go.

29
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:27,800
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: The Wrennick Hospitality dispute is getting worse and their lawyers sent a letter on Friday threatening to sue over the delayed rollout. I'd really rather we didn't announce cuts the same week.

30
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,533
Rufus Ashdown: Ugh. Okay. How much are they claiming?

31
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:39,733
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: They haven't put a number on it. Outside counsel at Pemberton Raike LLP think it's a negotiating posture.

32
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:41,933
Evander Wainscott: Is it material?

33
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:48,600
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Could be. Two to three percent of revenue if it went badly. I don't think it will.

34
00:03:48,800 --> 00:04:04,800
Jem Tolliver: Can I go back to the people side? Sorry. The Ashcombe Vale team. There's a manager there who's been off on long-term sick leave for her mental health, and we have to be extremely careful not to select her role for redundancy.

35
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,133
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Very careful. That's a claim waiting to happen.

36
00:04:09,333 --> 00:04:10,867
Jem Tolliver: Exactly.

37
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:15,200
Rufus Ashdown: Of course. Yeah. Who else knows about all this?

38
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:20,600
Jem Okonjo: Just this group and the board. And the comms agency, under NDA.

39
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,667
Rufus Ashdown: Which agency?

40
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:26,400
Jem Okonjo: Haverleigh & Stone. Same as last time.

41
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:30,133
Rufus Ashdown: Fine. So, okay, what's the comms plan?

42
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:46,067
Jem Tolliver: All-hands on the fourteenth, managers briefed the night before, letters same day. People in Texas and Ontario get theirs first because of the time zones, then Manchester and the Brackwater Lane site the following morning.

43
00:04:46,267 --> 00:04:52,533
Callum Wainscott: Please do not do it on a Friday. Fridays in general are fine, but not for this.

44
00:04:52,733 --> 00:04:54,733
Jem Tolliver: It's a Tuesday.

45
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:56,267
Callum Wainscott: Good.

46
00:04:56,467 --> 00:04:59,867
Evander Wainscott: And severance is budgeted at $1,250.

47
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:02,400
Rufus Ashdown: Okay. Anything else?

48
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:11,000
Eamon Delacroix-Bey: Just, everybody, nothing about the restructure in Slack or email, phone or in person only until it's announced.

49
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:16,267
Rufus Ashdown: Got it. Okay. Thanks all, this is hard stuff. Let's take ten.
